A minor note about burning messages: you can remove them using a wand
of cold. Also, trying to burn a message on an icy floor will *engrave*
rather than burning, as I recall.

> The two best things to use are wand of fire and an Atheme (like
> Magicbane). You can also burn a message in the floor with wand of
> lightning (one turn, same as fire), but blinds you for a while. The cool
> thing about engraving with an Atheme is that it doesn't get used up and
> takes only one turn. You can engrave with other weapons too, but they
> get dull (meaning a minus) and at -3 are too dull to engrave anymore.
> Hard gems also engrave, and don't get dull, but engraving with anything
> other than an Atheme takes more than one turn. You make graffiti with a
> magic marker (one turn). Last you can just write in the dust with most
> objects, or your finger (by pressing -). That also takes only one turn
> but as I said, smudges really fast.
>
> I said 4 main types because there are also messages scrawled in blood
> which smudge easy, and don't come up much anwyay.
>
Scrawling in blood is effectively the same as writing in the dust; just
a little cosmetic fancy for certain monsters. A useful list of Elbereth
information can be found at:
http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/elbereth_faq.html , including how to
engrave with a non-athame weapon (for emergencies only).



